\ ======================================================================
\ 01 — a tour. What the language does before any of the interesting parts.
\
\ Run:  make demos      (checks this against 01_tour.expected)
\ or:   ./_build/default/bin/catcat.exe -f demos/01_tour.cat
\
\ Every paragraph below is fed to the REPL as one line, so the transcript
\ you get back reads as a session. Comments are `\` to end of line.
\ ======================================================================

\ --- 1. Postfix arithmetic. The top of the stack is the RIGHT operand.

10 3 - show print "\n" print

\ --- 2. `define`. The signature is INFERRED; you do not have to write one.

define sq { dup * }

\ Writing one is an assertion, checked against what the body actually does.

define cube ( i64 -- i64 ) { dup dup * * }

7 sq show print "\n" print
3 cube show print "\n" print

\ A wrong assertion is rejected at the definition, not at the call.

define wrong ( i64 -- str ) { dup * }

\ --- 3. Named parameters. `$x` binds the top of the input segment.
\ They exist so that deep stack shuffling never has to be written by hand:
\ `dup`, `pop` and `swap` reach two slots and no composition of them reaches
\ a third.

define hypotsq ( $x:i64 $y:i64 -- i64 ) { $x $x * $y $y * + }

3 4 hypotsq show print "\n" print

\ --- 4. Conditionals. `if { cond } then { conseq } else { alt } endif`.
\ The condition block runs INLINE and leaves a bool; it may be empty when the
\ bool is already there.

define abs { dup 0 < if { } then { 0 swap - } endif }

-5 abs show print " " print
5 abs show print "\n" print

\ The branches must agree on what they leave behind, not on how they are
\ written. Here `then` is ( -- ) and the implicit `else` is ( i64 -- i64 );
\ framing the first by an i64 makes them agree.

define dec_if_big { dup 10 < if { } then { 1 - } endif }

\ Disagreeing on the result is what gets rejected.

define mismatch { dup 0 < if { } then { true } else { 1 } endif }

\ --- 5. Recursion. A word's own name is not in scope in its body; `recurse`
\ is. The signature is mandatory, because inferring the type of a word that
\ calls itself is solving a fixpoint.

define fact ( i64 -- i64 !Rec ) { dup 0 <= if { } then { pop 1 } else { dup 1 - recurse * } endif }

\ `!Rec` is what "may not terminate" looks like in a type, and it propagates.
\ A written stack effect does NOT mean the effects are written too — the row is
\ inferred unless some `!` appears, so this picks up `!Rec` without asking.

define fact10 ( -- i64 ) { 10 fact }

\ A bare `!` is how you assert there are none, and it is held to.

define pure10 ( -- i64 ! ) { 10 fact }

fact10 show print "\n" print

\ A loop is a tail call. The continuation does not grow.

define countdown ( $n:i64 -- !IO !Rec ) { $n 0 <= if { } then { } else { $n show print " " print $n 1 - recurse } endif }

5 countdown "\n" print

\ --- 6. Strings.

"catcat" " is " cat "concatenative" cat "\n" cat print

\ --- 7. `locate` decompiles a word from the core term. There is no source
\ text kept anywhere; what you see is what the elaborator produced.

locate hypotsq

locate abs
